<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65157" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαστ-ίζω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Nonn.
			<u>D.</u>
			2.645
		</span></i>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαστ-ίσδω</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
			7.108
		</span></i>: 
			Ep.
		
		aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάστιξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.768
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμαστίχθην</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.114
			</span></i>; part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαστιχθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.348
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i>): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάστιξ</span>):—<i>whip,
				flog</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάστιξεν δ᾽ ἵππους</span>
			Il.l.c., etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυ . . ὑπὸ . . ὤμους
				μαστίσδοιεν</span> (v. supr.) <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
			</span></i> l.c.: c. inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάστιξεν
				δ᾽ ἐλάαν</span>
			<i>whipped</i> them on or forward, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.366
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.82
			</span></i>, etc.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵνα . . σε πολλοὶ μαστίξωσι λόγοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					303.5
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Smyrna</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>stimulate</i> the bowels, <i><span class="en">
				Steph.
				<u>in Hp.</u>
				2.311
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				312
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>—
				Ep.
			 word, used twice in Com., <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				133.5
			</span></i>, also in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Nu.</u>
				22.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Wi.</u>
				5.11
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			); and in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				42
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pr.Im.</u>
				24
			</span></i>, etc.; the 
				Att.
			 form being <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαστιγόω</span>.</div>
